# What must never enter an image build context (#308).
#
# Why a ROOT .dockerignore and not only `Dockerfile.rsi-runner.dockerignore`:
# the per-Dockerfile form is honoured by BuildKit ONLY. The classic builder
# ignores it and falls back to this file — so with `DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0`, an old
# daemon, or any tool shelling out to `docker build` without BuildKit, every
# exclusion written there simply does not apply. The RSI runner copies this
# context into an image that then executes agent-authored code, so "the
# exclusions applied on my machine" is not a property worth relying on.
#
# The two files carry the same RULES (comments may differ), enforced by
# scripts/check-build-context.py.
#
# Nothing tracked by git is denied here. `**/data/` would have been the
# obvious rule to write and it would have stripped
# `packages/hive-conductor/backend/data/` and the BFCL benchmark corpus out of
# every image; the gate checks that too.

# ---- Secrets. The reason this file exists. -------------------------------
# `.env` holds the database password, the LiteLLM gateway key and every
# provider key the deployment has. `.env.example` is deliberately NOT denied:
# it ships as documentation and carries no value.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
gateway.env
**/gateway.env
*.pem
**/*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.age
**/*.age
.age-key*
recovery-phrase*
/secrets/
**/secrets/
# Top-level only: `**/vault/` would strip
# packages/maistro-core/tests/vault/ out of every image. An operator's vault
# directory lives at the root; a package named for the subsystem it tests does
# not stop being source because of its name.
/vault/

# ---- VCS metadata --------------------------------------------------------
# `.git` carries every secret ever committed and later removed, which is the
# whole point of history. The RSI runner bakes a fresh repo from the copied
# tree instead of inheriting one.
/.git

# ---- Virtual environments and caches ------------------------------------
# Large, host-specific, and `.venv` can hold credentials cached by tooling.
/.venv
**/.venv
/venv/
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
/.pytest_cache
/.mypy_cache
/.ruff_cache
/.hypothesis
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo

# ---- Build and test output ----------------------------------------------
**/dist
**/build
**/*.egg-info
**/.coverage
**/coverage.xml
**/htmlcov
bandit.json
semgrep.json

# ---- Local run data ------------------------------------------------------
# RSI reports hold exported patches, promotion records and scorecards from
# previous runs. Copying them in would hand a candidate the full history of
# every candidate before it.
/rsi-reports/
**/rsi-reports/
/.conductor/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
population.db

# ---- Editor and OS noise -------------------------------------------------
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp
/.idea/
/.vscode/
